  "step_2": "The individual states that, since there is no loss in either lottery (i.e., no negative outcomes), they choose the lottery with a lower probability of success but a higher payoff. This reflects a preference for a higher guaranteed gain (2500 vs. 2400) despite the lower probability (33% vs. 34%). The individual is explicitly justifying the choice based on the magnitude of the gain and the probability of success, not on any comparison of outcomes above an average. There is no mention of average outcomes, nor of counting outcomes above the average. The deliberation process focuses on the trade-off between gain size and probability, not on the number of outcomes exceeding a mean value. Thus, the described reasoning does not involve the specified decision reason.",
